MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273810] = {name = "Xalzaix's Awakening", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]Mythrax channels his energy into Xalzaix, awakening his living weapon. The energy generated causes 2 Oblivion Spheres to form.\n\n When the channel completes, Xalzaix erupts, inflicting 4701 Shadow damage and applying Annihilation to all players."}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273811] = {name = "Xalzaix's Awakening", additional_info = "Instant\n[q]Mythrax channels his energy into Xalzaix, awakening his living weapon. The energy generated causes 2 Oblivion Spheres to form.\n\n When the channel completes, Xalzaix erupts, inflicting 4701 Shadow damage and applying Annihilation to all players."}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273812] = {name = "Blowgun of the Sethra", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]The trolls of the desert who worshipped Sethraliss used these blowguns to hunt their prey, be it beast, or troll. The poison the darts were dipped in would paralyze their prey, and within a minute, kill them. \"The Prick of Sethraliss\" was whispered to children in order to keep them in line, as was written in an ancient poem: \"Should the young turn defiant, show anger or malice, the winds of Vol'Dun will bring the Prick of Sethraliss.\""}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273813] = {name = "Enthralled", additional_info = nil}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273814] = {name = "Follower: Falstad Wildhammer", additional_info = nil}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273815] = {name = "[q3]Croak Crock", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]During times of war, the Zandalari faced off against many powerful foes. Some, even, that they could not break. Their witchdoctors devised these cursed pots and through the use of powerful magic, summoned them at different locations within the enemy's encampment. Shortly after, a fountain of frogs would spring forth, causing a ruckus and confusing the enemy in the process. Little did they know that these frogs carried a plague with them that would quickly devastate their ranks and force them to retreat or surrender.\n[q3]Croak Crock\nBinds when picked up\nToy\n[q2]Use: Summon a plague of toads. (10 Min Cooldown)\n[q]\"Used to plague those who dared to cross the Zandalari.\""}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273816] = {name = "Follower: Arcanist Valtrois", additional_info = nil}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273817] = {name = "[q2]Intact Direhorn Hatchling", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]The Zandalari are regarded for their beast taming, and one of their greatest allies is that of the direhorn. Plated skin, with spikes protruding from various directions, this creature offered both protection for istelf and that of its master. It was custom for its future master to be the first to see it when it broke free from its shell.surrender.\n[q2]Intact Direhorn Egg\nBinds when picked up\n[q2]Use: Teaches you how to summon and dismiss a Direhorn Hatchling\n[q2]Right Click to summon and dismiss the Direhorn Hatchling.\n1 to 80 ( 80)"}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273818] = {name = "Child of Rezan", additional_info = nil}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273819] = {name = "[q3]Sanguinating Totem", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]After the great plague, there were still those who clung to the magics of the blood god. They tested their magics and perfected them. One such relic was a totem, which when concentrated upon, would drain not just the life from their enemies, but also their blood, infusing the caster with it and altering them in unusual ways. This was the dawn of who the Zandalari call, \"The Blood Trolls\".\n[q3]Sanguinating Totem\n[q7]Binds to Warband\nUnique-EquippedTrinket\n+6 Stamina\n[q2]Use: Drains health from an enemy, transferring it to the caster. (1 Min, 30 Sec Cooldown)\n45"}
