MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273851] = {name = "Soul Coffer", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]When a soul is called from the afterlife, it is free to roam the material realm if it is not restrained within moments of its arrival. The Drust created prisons for these souls for later use in their dark rituals, during which time the soul would suffer within Thros, and become a twisted version of what it once had been."}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273852] = {name = "[q3]Dance of the Dead", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]When the Drust wished to enchant the minds of their enemies, or prey, they would often do so subtly by leaving small tokens around their targets. Curious objects, when focused on by the holder, would summon a haunting vision of a dancing spectre. This spectre would entrance all who watched it, rendering them docile and easy to dispatch.\n[q3]Dance of the Dead\nBinds when picked up\nToy\n[q2]Use: Summons a ghostly dancing witch. (10 Min Cooldown)"}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273853] = {name = "Sandstorm", additional_info = "[q]Your spells and abilities have a chance to summon a cylone of piercing winds. Enemies inside the cyclone take 68 damage every 2, and deal 228 less damage to you."}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273854] = {name = "[q3]Restored Revenant", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]As the Drust became more skilled at trapping souls within objects, so did they become more adept at creating constructs of death in which to trap the souls. Revenants are amongst the fiercest of these creatures. Stripped of memory and any semblance of self, their bodies constructed from pieces that can no longer decompose, these creatures never tire and will hunt their prey for all eternity.\n[q3]Pile of Bones\nBinds when picked up\n[q2]Use: Teaches you how to summon and dismiss a Restored Revenant.\n[q2]Right Click to summon and dismiss your Restored Revenant.\n1 to 80 ( 80)"}
MultiLanguageSpellData['en'][273855] = {name = "[q3]Fetish of the Tormented Mind", additional_info = "2 sec cast\n[q]This fetish was paramount for twisting the minds of their enemies, causing doubt to grow like a weed within the target, encroaching brighter thoughts. Those afflicted would question their motivations, their ideals, or their courage and would often find themselves at the end of a Drust blade before finally rediscovering their resolve.\n[q3]Fetish of the Tormented Mind\n[q7]Binds to Warband\nUnique-EquippedTrinket\n+6 Stamina\n[q2]Use: Slow your current enemy target's attack and casting speed by 15% for 5 sec. (1 Min, 30 Sec Cooldown)\n45"}
